pitest (2.2.1-1+deb12+1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  pitest switches from major version 1 to major version 2 for bookworm
  (1.9.1 -> 2.2.1).

  Increasing the major version introduces breaking changes. The following
  breaking changes are introduced with this update:

  - The "-f" flag for the "piTest" command *must* be preceded with the
    "--module" flag to specify which extension module should be updated. The
    module address "0" is no longer a valid address.
    Calling "piTest" with only the "-f" flag to update any extension module is
    not possible any more.
  - The exit status for the "piTest" command is set properly when the command
    terminates. This means that an error makes "piTest" exit with an exit
    status that isn't "0" to indicate that an error occurred. Checking for the
    exit status is the preferred way to detect whether "piTest" encountered an
    error.
    Please check for any uses of "piTest" in scripts that evaluate the exit
    status when calling "piTest", and for any changes in how these scripts
    might behave due to this change.

  Introducing these breaking changes is necessary to also introduce the
  following, very important features and quality of life improvements
  surrounding the firmware update of extension modules:

  - Allow rescuing an extension module from a failed firmware update with the
    "--rescue" flag.
  - More descriptive error messages are printed on standard error when "piTest"
    encounters an error.

  We believe introducing these breaking changes for the mentioned addition of
  better firmware update as well as being able rescue extension modules for
  which a firmware update failed is a worth trade off.

  More information on how to use "piTest" can be found in the "piTest(1)"
  manual page (viewable from a terminal with the command "man 1 piTest"), and
  about firmware updates in the official Revolution Pi documentation:
  https://revolutionpi.com/en/docs/firmware-updates

 -- Thomas Böhler <t.boehler@kunbus.com>  Thu, 01 Sep 2026 14:22:18 +0200

pitest (1.8.1-1+deb12+1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  Updated picontrol to version 2.3.6.

  Fixed an issue where the names of some virtual devices were displayed incorrectly. 

 -- Ramiro Gsponer <r.gsponer@kunbus.com>  Mon, 02 Jun 2025 12:11:12 +0200

pitest (1.8.0-1+deb12+1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  The --force flag has been introduced to allow a firmware update even if the current firmware
  version is equal to or older than the one running on the module.

  A spinner has been added to provide visual feedback while a firmware update is in progress,
  improving the user experience and making the process more intuitive.

  The manual page has been updated to reflect the new features and options, with clearer
  instructions on how to specify and update individual modules.

 -- Ramiro Gsponer <r.gsponer@kunbus.com>  Thu, 27 Mar 2025 15:45:24 +0100
